Chapter: PlugLambdaSubject

 A lambda subject for the source plugs, kept OUT of `codex/test` on purpose:
 that tree is a battery tier and this is a probe, not a test.

 Five shapes, because a plug can pass one and fail the next. Immediate
 application needs only substitution. A let-bound lambda applied twice needs a
 name. A lambda capturing a local, and one capturing a parameter, are what
 defeat plain lifting: the captured value has to travel to the lifted
 procedure. A lambda passed AS AN ARGUMENT is the shape that lifting alone
 cannot close, because the callee receives a value and not a call site, which
 is why zig carries `CxFn1`..`CxFn4` closure structs rather than lifting.

Section: Shapes

  immediate : Integer -> Integer
  immediate (n) = (\x -> x + 100) n

  bound-twice : Integer -> Integer
  bound-twice (n) = let f = \x -> x * 3 in f n + f (n + 3)

  captures-local : Integer -> Integer
  captures-local (n) = let c = n * 2 in (\x -> x + c) 7

  captures-param : Integer -> Integer
  captures-param (n) = (\x -> x + n) 1

  apply-twice : (Integer -> Integer), Integer -> Integer
  apply-twice (f) (n) = f (f n)

  passed-as-value : Integer -> Integer
  passed-as-value (n) = apply-twice (\x -> x + 1) n

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (show (immediate 5))
   print-line-uni (show (bound-twice 2))
   print-line-uni (show (captures-local 5))
   print-line-uni (show (captures-param 41))
   print-line-uni (show (passed-as-value 5))
  end
